WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.181 --> 00:00:18.442
creature's face disappeared into the bushes.

2
00:00:19.443 --> 00:00:21.304
The children bent over the caretaker.

3
00:00:21.324 --> 00:00:23.745
"He's not dead, is he?"

4
00:00:24.185 --> 00:00:25.445
Jimmy asked anxiously.

5
00:00:25.465 --> 00:00:28.507
"Just hurt," said Kathleen.

6
00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:31.588
"He's very handsome, don't you think?"

7
00:00:33.028 --> 00:00:35.009
"Oh yes," agreed Mabel.

8
00:00:35.029 --> 00:00:39.092
"Quite a nice young man," said a voice behind them.

9
00:00:40.012 --> 00:00:41.013
The children looked up.

10
00:00:41.773 --> 00:00:43.955
And there was the middle-aged Ugly-Wugly.

11
00:00:44.935 --> 00:00:46.656
Everyone but Gerald screamed.

12
00:00:48.097 --> 00:00:50.738
He was still wearing the ring, so he wasn't afraid.

13
00:00:51.979 --> 00:00:53.560
But he noticed something strange.

14
00:00:55.381 --> 00:01:00.024
The middle-aged Ugly-Wugly's face was no longer made of paper—it was real.

15
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.021
And so were his arms and legs.

16
00:01:06.263 --> 00:01:09.165
Somehow this creature had really come alive!

17
00:01:09.185 --> 00:01:11.587
"What happened to the caretaker?"

18
00:01:12.047 --> 00:01:12.888
Gerald asked him.

19
00:01:12.908 --> 00:01:17.031
"It was most unfortunate," said the Ugly-Wugly.

20
00:01:17.051 --> 00:01:20.734
"The others must have lost their way in the passage last night.

21
00:01:21.054 --> 00:01:22.295
They never found the hotel."

22
00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.537
"Did you find it?"

23
00:01:24.937 --> 00:01:26.298
Gerald said in surprise.

24
00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:28.100
"Of course.

25
00:01:28.636 --> 00:01:33.058
I wandered through the passage until I found the very nice hotel, just as you said.

26
00:01:34.759 --> 00:01:37.780
When I found the others again, they were behind this door.

27
00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.021
They were angry.

28
00:01:39.521 --> 00:01:42.102
They'd been here all night, trying to get out."

29
00:01:44.463 --> 00:01:46.544
Jimmy's eyes were wide with fear.

30
00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:50.946
"Here, take the ring," Gerald whispered.

31
00:01:51.926 --> 00:01:54.848
Jimmy put on the ring and instantly looked braver.

32
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.662
"But what happened to the caretaker?"

33
00:01:59.062 --> 00:02:00.023
Gerald asked again.

34
00:02:03.826 --> 00:02:05.027
suddenly opened the door.

35
00:02:05.448 --> 00:02:08.450
Before I could protect him, the man in the top hat hit him.

36
00:02:09.031 --> 00:02:11.033
I was just going for help when you arrived."

37
00:02:11.053 --> 00:02:16.217
"We must find the others," said Gerald.

38
00:02:16.237 --> 00:02:21.242
"They've gone to bathe in the lake," said the Ugly-Wugly.

39
00:02:21.262 --> 00:02:23.524
"Their clothes are in the woods."

40
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:29.563
Kathleen and Jimmy went to check on the other Ugly-Wuglies.

41
00:02:30.844 --> 00:02:33.926
Gerald and Mabel stayed behind to tend to the caretaker.

42
00:02:35.268 --> 00:02:37.770
The Ugly-Wugly sat down on the temple steps.

43
00:02:39.571 --> 00:02:42.173
In the woods Jimmy found four heaps of clothing.

44
00:02:43.475 --> 00:02:46.117
There were broomsticks, hockey sticks, and masks.

45
00:02:47.478 --> 00:02:50.040
All these things had made up the Ugly-Wugly men.

46
00:02:50.961 --> 00:02:54.104
Kathleen found the two ladies sitting on a bench in the sun.

47
00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:56.961
But they had no life in them.

48
00:02:59.082 --> 00:03:00.463
Jimmy shook them to pieces.

49
00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:11.170
spell is broken."

50
00:03:11.711 --> 00:03:13.232
Kathleen sighed with relief.

51
00:03:15.113 --> 00:03:16.994
They went back to the Temple of Flora.

52
00:03:17.875 --> 00:03:19.636
The caretaker was trying to sit up.

53
00:03:20.657 --> 00:03:25.220
Gerald told the Ugly-Wugly to hide in the bushes so he wouldn't frighten the caretaker.

54
00:03:29.748 --> 00:03:32.751
"Jimmy is the best one to go with you," said Gerald.

55
00:03:34.052 --> 00:03:36.193
That was true because Jimmy had the ring.

56
00:03:37.615 --> 00:03:39.957
The children helped the caretaker to his feet.

57
00:03:39.977 --> 00:03:42.519
"Are you sure you're all right?"

58
00:03:42.919 --> 00:03:43.740
Mabel asked him.

59
00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:47.443
"Yes. But I had the strangest dream."

60
00:03:48.303 --> 00:03:49.084
He looked around.

61
00:03:49.104 --> 00:03:52.847
"I'm grateful for your help.

62
00:03:53.187 --> 00:03:54.709
You may visit here whenever you like."

63
00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.472
They all shook hands, and the caretaker walked away.

64
00:04:01.688 --> 00:04:05.532
"We have to get rid of that Ugly-Wugly," said Kathleen.

65
00:04:05.552 --> 00:04:07.173
"But how?"

66
00:04:07.654 --> 00:04:08.334
asked Gerald.

67
00:04:08.354 --> 00:04:11.617
"He became real inside the passage.

68
00:04:12.078 --> 00:04:17.462
If we could just get him back there Suddenly Jimmy came out of the bushes.

69
00:04:17.483 --> 00:04:22.067
"The Ugly-Wugly is taking a walk," Jimmy said.

70
00:04:22.087 --> 00:04:27.592
"He says he's a very rich businessman and he needs to get to London."

71
00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:32.542
Gerald and the girls were still planning how to get rid of the Ugly-Wugly.

72
00:04:33.422 --> 00:04:35.223
But Jimmy wasn't paying attention.

73
00:04:35.243 --> 00:04:39.524
"He has a car and a tennis court.

74
00:04:39.885 --> 00:04:42.305
I wish I were rich," said Jimmy.

75
00:04:42.325 --> 00:04:47.127
"I'd spend my money on "Oh no!"

76
00:04:47.628 --> 00:04:49.428
cried the girls, looking at Jimmy.

77
00:04:50.469 --> 00:04:53.310
Suddenly he was growing rich right in front of them.

78
00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.091
But he was also growing older.

79
00:04:57.031 --> 00:04:59.932
When the changes stopped, the girls gasped.

80
00:04:59.952 --> 00:05:03.502
"Do you know the way to the train station?"

81
00:05:03.943 --> 00:05:05.387
asked rich, old Jimmy.
